  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1221 PM CDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nNorthwest flow will bring scattered thunderstorms forming in New \nMexico into the western half of our CWA Wednesday night into the \nearly hours of Thursday. A similar setup will bring additional\nchances for storms on Thursday afternoon and evening, especially\nwest of I-27. Temperatures will continue to cool through the end \nof the week. Low temperatures will drop mainly into the high 60s \nwith high temperatures near seasonal normal Thursday and Friday. \nThis cooling period will be brief as warmer and drier conditions \nwill return Saturday with upper ridging redeveloping, causing \ntemperatures to return to triple digits east of I-27 during the \nweekend and early next week across the region.",
